---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import styles from '../styles/legal.module.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Copyright & Content Policy | WitrQuran"
  description="Copyright & Content Policy for WitrQuran, explaining how content rights and open source software are handled."
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class={styles.pageContainer}>
    <nav class={styles.breadcrumb} aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span>Copyright &amp; Content Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <header class={styles.header}>
      <h1 class={styles.title}>Copyright &amp; Content Policy</h1>
      <p class={styles.lastUpdated}>Last Updated: September 27, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class={styles.content}>
      <p>WitrQuran is a free and open source Quran listening platform created to make listening to the Quran simple fast and free from unnecessary distractions</p>

      <p>The Quran is the Book of Almighty Allah SWT</p>

      <p>WitrQuran does not claim to create author modify or own the Quran</p>

      <p>This policy explains how copyright and content rights are handled on WitrQuran</p>

      <h2>1. Quran</h2>

      <p>The Quran is the revelation of Almighty Allah SWT</p>

      <p>WitrQuran does not claim ownership over the Quran itself</p>

      <p>WitrQuran is simply a platform created to make listening to the Quran easier for everyone by the will of Allah SWT</p>

      <h2>2. Quran Recitation Audio</h2>

      <p>The Quran recitation audio available through WitrQuran is provided through an external source</p>

      <p>The audio was not recorded or produced by WitrQuran</p>

      <p>WitrQuran does not claim ownership of the underlying recitation recordings</p>

      <p>Any copyright or related rights associated with third party recordings remain with their respective owners or licensors</p>

      <h2>3. WitrQuran Source Code</h2>

      <p>The WitrQuran software is open source and released under the <strong>MIT License</strong></p>

      <p>The source code can be publicly inspected modified and redistributed subject to the terms of the MIT License</p>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View WitrQuran on GitHub</a></p>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran/blob/main/LICENSE?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the MIT License</a></p>

      <p>The MIT License applies to the WitrQuran source code and does not automatically apply to third party audio content or other third party resources</p>

      <h2>4. Third Party Content</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran may provide access to or rely upon content and services supplied by third parties</p>

      <p>Third party content may have separate copyright licenses terms of use or usage restrictions</p>

      <p>The presence of third party content on WitrQuran does not mean that WitrQuran owns that content</p>

      <p>Users should respect the applicable rights and terms associated with third party content</p>

      <h2>5. Copyright Complaints</h2>

      <p>If you believe that content made available through WitrQuran infringes your copyright or other intellectual property rights you can report the matter to us</p>

      <p>Please provide enough information for us to understand and investigate the complaint</p>

      <p>A useful report should include:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Your full name</li>
        <li>Your contact information</li>
        <li>Identification of the copyrighted work</li>
        <li>Identification of the content you believe infringes your rights</li>
        <li>The location of the relevant content</li>
        <li>An explanation of why you believe the content infringes your rights</li>
        <li>Any supporting information that may help us review the matter</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Copyright complaints can be submitted through our designated contact channel</p>

      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contact Faruk on Instagram</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contact Faruk on LinkedIn</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p>You may also contact:</p>

      <p><strong><a href="mailto:witrfaruk@proton.me">witrfaruk@proton.me</a></strong></p>

      <h2>6. Review of Reports</h2>

      <p>When a copyright or content complaint is received we may review the information provided and investigate the reported material</p>

      <p>Depending on the circumstances we may:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Request additional information</li>
        <li>Remove or restrict access to the reported content</li>
        <li>Contact the relevant third party</li>
        <li>Take other appropriate action</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Submitting a complaint does not automatically guarantee removal</p>

      <p>Each report may require individual review</p>

      <h2>7. False or Misleading Claims</h2>

      <p>Please do not submit knowingly false fraudulent or misleading copyright complaints</p>

      <p>Abuse of the reporting process may result in the complaint being disregarded</p>

      <h2>8. Content Accuracy</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran is designed specifically as a Quran listening platform</p>

      <p>We do not provide translations commentary or independent religious interpretations</p>

      <p>If you believe that Quranic audio or related content is incorrect or technically affected please report the issue so that it can be reviewed</p>

      <h2>9. User Submitted Material</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran currently does not provide a system for users to publicly upload or publish their own content</p>

      <p>There are no public user profiles comments posts or community submissions</p>

      <p>Any information voluntarily provided through contact or reporting channels is used only for the purpose for which it was submitted</p>

      <h2>10. Copyright in WitrQuran</h2>

      <p>The WitrQuran website software and original materials created specifically for the project may be protected by applicable intellectual property laws</p>

      <p>The source code is separately licensed under the MIT License</p>

      <p>Third party content remains subject to the rights and licenses of its respective owners</p>

      <h2>11. Respecting Intellectual Property</h2>

      <p>We respect copyright and intellectual property rights</p>

      <p>If you believe something available through WitrQuran should not be available or requires additional authorization please contact us rather than attempting to resolve the matter through unauthorized access or disruption of the service</p>

      <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>

      <p>We may update this Copyright &amp; Content Policy when the website content sources licensing arrangements or applicable requirements change</p>

      <p>The <strong>Last Updated</strong> date will be updated when material changes are made</p>

      <h2>13. Contact</h2>

      <p>For copyright concerns content questions or intellectual property matters contact:</p>

      <p><strong>Md Faruk Abdulla</strong></p>

      <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:witrfaruk@proton.me">witrfaruk@proton.me</a></p>

      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WitrQuran GitHub Repository</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Faruk on GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Faruk on LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Faruk on Instagram</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p><strong>The Quran is from Almighty Allah SWT. WitrQuran is simply a tool created to make listening easier for everyone by His will.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
